  "verbalization": "Ixerisoside A is implicated in the regulation of Protein kinase C eta through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Ixerisoside A acts as a target of several compounds, which in turn interact with Protein kinase C eta. Specifically, Ixerisoside A is linked to Endothelial lipase, which is targeted by a complex compound, and this compound further targets Protein kinase C eta. Similarly, Ixerisoside A is also linked to SK-MEL-28, a cell line that is targeted by another compound, which also targets Protein kinase C eta. These findings collectively indicate that Ixerisoside A may exert its effects through a mechanism involving the modulation of Protein kinase C eta, possibly through the activation or inhibition of downstream signaling pathways. The evidence supports a potential role for Ixerisoside A in influencing the activity of Protein kinase C eta, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
